# Build context for .devcontainer/Dockerfile, the one build whose context is
# the repository root (docker-compose.yml, context '..'). The image consumes
# only .devcontainer/, so the context is allowlisted to exactly that: the
# upload stays small no matter what generated state (zig-out, Rust targets,
# node_modules) accumulates in the tree, and a new cache directory never needs
# a row here.
*
!.devcontainer/
!.devcontainer/**
# The per-host env file is compose input on the host, never image input.
.devcontainer/.env
